    36	\begin{abstract}
    37	In this paper the 3-way intersection problem for $S(2,4,v)$ designs is investigated. Let $b_{v}=\frac {v(v-1)}{12}$ and $I_{3}[v]=\{0,1,\dots,b_{v}\}\setminus\{b_{v}-7,b_{v}-6,b_{v}-5,b_{v}-4,b_{v}-3,b_{v}-2,b_{v}-1\}$.
    38	Let $J_{3}[v]=\{k|$ there exist three $S(2,4,v)$ designs with $k$ same common blocks$\}$.
    39	We show that $J_{3}[v]\subseteq I_{3}[v]$ for any positive integer $v\equiv1, 4\ (\rm mod \ 12)$ and $J_{3}[v]=I_{3}[v]$, for $ v\geq49$ and $v=13 $.
    40	We find $J_{3}[16]$ completely.
    41	Also we determine some values of $J_{3}[v]$ for $\ v=25,28,37$ and 40.
    42	\end{abstract}
    43	\hspace*{-2.7mm} {\bf KEYWORDS:} {  \sf 3-way intersection; $S(2,4,v)$ design; GDD; trade}
