codex
The successful replies confirm the problem is not merely failing at small presets: both vendors returned exact answers at `hard`, and both scored calls at `n=6` also succeeded. The family’s selector always has at most five outer and seven filling runs, so increasing `n` only enlarges integer multipliers and the hypothetical expanded designs; it never adds a new structural step. Further escalation would turn this into large-integer bookkeeping, not a harder decomposition insight.

I’m therefore recording an H rejection. G and V are sound, Track A is inapplicable, and the attempted Track B route was defeated through the three prescribed escalations. I’ll preserve the prototype under the required `rejected_gen_…` name with the script-owned transcript intact.
