Rejected on hardness, not correctness.

The [paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/1301.4764) gives an exact additive construction, so G and V pass. However, Track A is unsupported and the Track B candidate was solved at every tested level:

- Easy: 2/3
- Medium: 3/3
- Hard: 2/3
- Escalated `n=6`: 2/2 scored calls

Further calls hit HTTP 403 quota errors, which were not counted. Increasing `n` only enlarges arithmetic operands; the compact route remains the same twelve-ingredient calculation.

Deliverables:

- [REJECTED.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1301.4764/REJECTED.md)
- [Preserved rejected generator](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1301.4764/rejected_gen_1301_4764.py)
- [Oracle transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1301.4764/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [Local gate report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1301.4764/selftest_report.json)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1301.4764/README.md)

The final regression passed all nine local gates. No shipping `gen_1301_4764.py` remains, as required for a rejected prototype.
